# `const first: string[] = rows[0].split(",")`: the call and the cast stand in the stretch of a guess at `rows[0]`, and behind the rejoin the cast alone is read: it is bound anew there, and the call stays bound to what the typed arm has built, which does not dominate the loop
# the row in front of the loop asks the list by the name that enters the loop. It was UseNotDominated at the IsPristine.
# f2 = countsCellsThatAgree, f1 = countsEmptyCells
